From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dbSta: store the timing constraints in the .odb

write_db stores the current timing constraints in the block; read_db -sdc
restores them and returns 1, or 0 if the .odb carries none. The
constraints are stored in a native, id-based, canonically ordered record
(pins as dbBTerm / dbITerm ids, no names, no Tcl) that restores in time
linear in the number of objects; an Sdc with constructs the native
encoder does not cover (generated clocks, derating, environment, ...)
falls back to the write_sdc text, replayed through Tcl.
ord::sdc_in_db_kind reports which form the current block carries:
native, text or none. Whether the native form can carry an Sdc is decided
by inspecting the Sdc through its public accessors, not by writing and
scanning text, so write_db stays cheap.

Guarantees, each with a regression test in src/dbSta/test (sdc_in_db1..9):
write_sdc after a restore is byte-identical to write_sdc before it; two
write_db of the same design, and a write_db after read_db -sdc in a fresh
process, produce byte-identical .odb files; an .odb without constraints
restores nothing and returns 0; restore runs only after a complete
read_db.

This is OpenROAD PR #11260 (branch sdc-in-odb on the oharboe fork),
squashed. Carried in bazel-orfs, together with the ORFS patch that
consumes it (patches/0052-orfs-sdc-in-odb-retire.patch), until the upstream PR
merges; retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that carries it. The
binary test fixture src/dbSta/test/sdc_in_db.odb is left out of the
carried copy: bazel's patch tool cannot apply binary diffs, and the
regression tests are not built here.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
